Why: telemetry landed today shows the repair drafter returns a verbatim old_string in about half of responses even though the prompt asks for a line range, and ANCHOR-MISS was observed on 2 of 6 repair attempts. A common cause is indentation: the model reproduces the statement but not its leading whitespace, so an exact substring test fails on text that is present in the file. This looks for exactly one line whose trimmed content equals the trimmed anchor and, when there is exactly one such line, replaces the anchor with that line's real text so the following exact-match test succeeds. It is deliberately conservative: it requires a UNIQUE match and a non-empty anchor, so it cannot mislocalise, and when no unique match exists it logs ANCHOR-MISS exactly as before.

The only new identifiers are the two block-scoped constants __wantAnchor and __anchorCands. Do not redeclare cur, curContent, fix, fv or ef, which already exist in scope. Do not modify any numeric literal.

